\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 The ceremony ended and the room went back to being a bar.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It did not thin out. Nothing in the Clambake ever thinned out; it only redistributed, and it redistributed now into a slow churn between the spa bath and the bar, with a hard eddy where the two currents met and nobody could get through holding a full glass. The staircase was occupied to the turn. The mezzanine was occupied. There were Elvi up there who had not been able to see any of it and had cheered every word.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It was a wake and it was a coronation and nobody had told the room which one to be, so it was being both, a few metres apart. Two Blue Hawaiis were laughing so hard that one had to take the other\u8217 ?s sleeve to stay upright. Close enough to touch them, a Tulsa wept into a beer with somebody\u8217 ?s hand flat on the back of his neck, and neither party found the other odd.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Sarah stayed where she was, because standing up was a project with stages and an audience, and because there was no need to. The room came past her. They came in ones and twos with their hands already half out, and every second one wanted to touch the belly, and about a third asked first.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy went into it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 She had not come with a plan. She had come to a wake with a bag she had not opened, and there was a thing at the back of her head that had been sitting there since Bent Street and had never once arranged itself into a question. It was less a suspicion than a set of pieces in a drawer: what she had found in the blood of the dead, and what she had never found in the blood of anybody who was well, on account of nobody who is well ever giving you any.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 The room was full of people who were well.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 So she circulated, in the way a woman circulates at a party, and what she was actually doing was getting sleeves pushed up.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 A Clambake with grey coming through his sideburns got himself off the chesterfield in three separate movements, with a hand on the arm of it and a sound. Two paces further on, an Elvine came up off a bar stool and stood a moment with her palm pressed flat into the small of her back, waiting for something to finish. Nobody looked at either of them. In that room it was weather.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Then Rusty Martin came off a low stool in one go, still talking, and went to the bar.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy did not stop walking. Her head turned, though, and stayed turned a beat past where it had any business.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Maile Duval had her sleeve pushed up past the elbow and her arm out and a small audience for it, and she was delighted.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?[ ] years,\u8221 ? she was saying. \u8220 ?[ ] years I\u8217 ?ve had that, and I went to a man in Bent Street about getting it taken off and he told me it\u8217 ?d cost more than the wedding did.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Let me,\u8221 ? said Kathy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Maile put the arm into her hands with the satisfaction of a woman who has finally found somebody qualified to agree with her. There had been a name on the inside of the forearm once, done in the ornate lettering that takes a good hand and a long sitting. It was a grey suggestion now. The heavy work at the edges had held on better than the rest, so what was left was an outline with the middle gone out of it, like a word rubbed off a blackboard by somebody in a hurry.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?When did it start going?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?That\u8217 ?s what I can\u8217 ?t tell you. I looked at his name every morning of my life and then one morning I\u8217 ?m at the sink and I think, hang on.\u8221 ? She turned the wrist over, pleased with herself. \u8220 ?Best thing that\u8217 ?s happened to me all year, and I\u8217 ?m counting getting out of Bent Street.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy turned the arm slightly, into the light off the bar, and did not let go of it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Any scars?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?What?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Anything you\u8217 ?ve had a long time. Old ones.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Maile thought about it, and then pushed the sleeve the rest of the way up, to a place above the elbow where there was nothing whatever to see, and looked at the nothing for a while with a different face on.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Huh,\u8221 ? she said.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy gave the arm back. She did it gently, and she was already looking past her.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It was not the same on all of them. The woman beside Maile Duval had a forearm you could still read. Dianne Carter, two along, had one you would have to be told was there. Some of them were further into it than others, and there was nothing in any of their faces to say which.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy came back to the dais with nothing in her hands and sat down next to Hayley, who had not moved and had not written anything down.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Say something to me,\u8221 ? said Kathy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?About what?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?About that lot. I want to hear it out loud and I don\u8217 ?t want to be the one who says it first.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?They were at Bent Street,\u8221 ? said Hayley.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?So were a lot of people who aren\u8217 ?t here.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?They were at Bent Street, and they\u8217 ?re the only ones in this room you\u8217 ?d look at twice.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?It isn\u8217 ?t pathogenic,\u8221 ? Kathy said. \u8220 ?That\u8217 ?s what I keep coming back to. Whatever\u8217 ?s in them isn\u8217 ?t making them ill. It\u8217 ?s the other thing. It\u8217 ?s salutogenic.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Hayley looked at her.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?It\u8217 ?s a word,\u8221 ? said Kathy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?I\u8217 ?m sure it is.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?It means it goes through you and tidies up.\u8221 ? She put both hands flat on her knees. \u8220 ?Something\u8217 ?s in them, it\u8217 ?s been in some of them longer than others, and it did not get there out of the air.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Who\u8217 ?s got what?\u8221 ? said Chanta, from the edge of the dais, with an Elvisette working on his shoulders and a beer he had not asked for.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Nobody answered him.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Hayley turned round slowly and looked at what was behind him. Betty Lee\u8217 ?s hair had gone entirely back to blonde at the roots. Marguerita, who had complained about that knee for [ ], had done the splits at a party and had not yet stopped telling people about it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?How long have they been with you?\u8221 ? said Hayley.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Depends which.\u8221 ? Chanta brightened, pleased to be asked something he could answer. \u8220 ?Betty\u8217 ?s ages. Marguerita, ooh. Bit less.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?And the ones by the curtains. Dianne and that lot.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Yeah, they\u8217 ?re lovely.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?How lovely?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Very lovely.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Chanta.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?They\u8217 ?re very lovely,\u8221 ? said Chanta, with the emphasis of a man being asked to repeat himself for no reason he could see, and then, because he was constitutionally unable to leave a silence alone, and because a corner of him had spent his whole life waiting for somebody in authority to ask him a question he could answer, he filled it. \u8220 ?All of them, if you want the truth. Every one of them. I\u8217 ?m not proud of it. Well. I\u8217 ?m a bit proud of it.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Nobody said anything.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It took about two seconds, which in a room that size is a long time. Hayley got there first, because it was her job. Kathy got there next and put both hands over her mouth. Sarah, from the chair, turned her head very slowly towards the curtains.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Walter got there before Chanta did, and Walter was already grinning like a split melon.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Chanta looked round at the faces.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?What,\u8221 ? he said.\
